 {:db/id "q-80766" :question/id #uuid "f63374b4-82d5-5092-bcef-8ec87e149ab1" :question/math-academy-id "q-80766" :question/problem "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b$, if \n\n$$\n{f}_{x}(x,y)=y(1+x){e}^{x}+ax{y}^{3}+3{x}^{2},\\,{f}_{y}(x,y)=bx{e}^{x}-3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the mixed partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y(1+x){e}^{x}+ax{y}^{3}+3{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =(1+x){e}^{x}+3ax{y}^{2}+0 \\\\  & =(1+x){e}^{x}+3ax{y}^{2} \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(bx{e}^{x}-3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =b(1+x){e}^{x}-6x{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. Hence, we have the identity\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1+x){e}^{x}+3ax{y}^{2}=b(1+x){e}^{x}-6x{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $(1+x){e}^{x}$ and $x{y}^{2},$ respectively, we see that $b=1$ and $a=-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80766/ma-source-field/bb9a738e393679ac0b913f685719c5da3264955182f0faf4b33c0d90689b3cd0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
