 {:db/id "q-8171" :question/id #uuid "0508a683-ff80-5adf-84b7-14d7f45257c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-8171" :question/problem "Find the first four non-zero terms of the Maclaurin expansion of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The standard Maclaurin expansion for $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4!}-\\frac{{x}^{6}}{6!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $\\sqrt{x}$ in the above expansion and simplifying gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{x} & =1-\\frac{(\\sqrt{x})^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{(\\sqrt{x})^{4}}{4!}-\\frac{(\\sqrt{x})^{6}}{6!}+⋯ \\\\  & =1-\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{24}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{720}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8171/ma-source-field/6c6e44ba68a265460b9830b558469defc65734aacee321a690950c8a3e101e38"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
