 {:db/id "q-81863" :question/id #uuid "b338b5cf-801c-50c4-9622-d9ab0fa4da90" :question/math-academy-id "q-81863" :question/problem "Find the maximum value of $f(x)=4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}-3)+2.$" :question/worked-solution "The range of the function $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nHorizontal and vertical shifts and stretches do not affect the range of a logarithmic function.\n\nTherefore, the range of the given function is $f(x)\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ and the function has no maximum value." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-81863/ma-source-field/592ce76d58f12b2bdc2d12a4c3c07a9e68b27a6a184e2c350c8d0bf275133eda"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
