 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "929e0321-87ad-5ccc-a7b5-9aeb909c70ea"] :question/problem "Find the contrapositive of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** it is not warm outside, **then** you need a jacket." :question/worked-solution "In our conditional statement: \n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ It is not warm outside.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ You need a jacket.\n\nThe contrapositive of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬B⇒¬A.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ It is warm outside.\n\n- $¬B:$ You don't need a jacket.\n\nTherefore, the contrapositive is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If you don't need a jacket, then it is warm outside." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-81985/ma-source-field/4d0d718aaf670ce3976364c9675fc4ebf011d46e05f6543ed2b9e3ab6df567e2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
