 {:db/id "q-82627" :question/id #uuid "370105fd-4191-5aeb-88c5-e95f00d93193" :question/math-academy-id "q-82627" :question/problem "Find the converse of the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ **If** it is not snowing, **then** it is not winter." :question/worked-solution "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ It is not snowing.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ It is not winter.\n\nThe converse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\nB⇒A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the converse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If it is not winter, then it is not snowing." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-82627/ma-source-field/8e629c310f5f2ed4ed14877dfd5211929bb0b7f8378f753401f037c9c77afa59"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
