 {:db/id "q-82630" :question/id #uuid "89a8d37a-6c72-523d-8fc0-d006e8d4daf6" :question/math-academy-id "q-82630" :question/problem "Find the converse of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** you are not watching TV, **then** you are listening to music." :question/worked-solution "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ You are not watching TV.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ You are listening to music.\n\nThe converse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\nB⇒A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the converse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If you are listening to music, then you are not watching TV." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-82630/ma-source-field/6dd27cce1ab647f32628e2e3552116ffa3ae0e14143546518986d21c88ff5f17"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
