 {:db/id "q-83001" :question/id #uuid "edbfe110-6f37-5a51-8f96-227364b973f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-83001" :question/problem "Identify the sentence that is equivalent to the following: \"The cup is red and it is new.\"" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the sentence more concisely:\n\n\"The cup is red and new.\"\n\nUsing the commutative law, we can swap the order of the words \"red\" and \"new.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"The cup is new and red.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-83001/ma-source-field/be949ce1676de0d1eb84b6c97b3ddbeef8a3572ff77f5e6cc5e0b1d68d0a437a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
