 {:db/id "q-8360/ma-source-field/dbd2b59b6454b3931876586d49499d59f1b8a6fdea15a150a89978379dccba11" :answer-field/id #uuid "29d75aab-799f-5138-9f8f-42b050f51ab1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-8360/ma-source-field/dbd2b59b6454b3931876586d49499d59f1b8a6fdea15a150a89978379dccba11/49b485b8941c020b9a07ddd9c23b82e25263f7e5dabb0e927427c13f968bdf36" "q-8360/ma-source-field/dbd2b59b6454b3931876586d49499d59f1b8a6fdea15a150a89978379dccba11/ce9ba74438413506836630f0da3c7d4192d74e42ecb4b8a45252e6ec597924d5" "q-8360/ma-source-field/dbd2b59b6454b3931876586d49499d59f1b8a6fdea15a150a89978379dccba11/07a360a82ba6e5a7c8b552d8bd23520c8119df942c8a411fffccd6630e7efe7c" "q-8360/ma-source-field/dbd2b59b6454b3931876586d49499d59f1b8a6fdea15a150a89978379dccba11/425b53ace7668c2430e484a02d79bf6cedc6f35e70cd4b51ba12804778874d0a" "q-8360/ma-source-field/dbd2b59b6454b3931876586d49499d59f1b8a6fdea15a150a89978379dccba11/b0f265024022f22dedbdd1bdc7df3a760933457d3ea34c80d11a6fc946828d1b"] :answer-field/correct "q-8360/ma-source-field/dbd2b59b6454b3931876586d49499d59f1b8a6fdea15a150a89978379dccba11/ce9ba74438413506836630f0da3c7d4192d74e42ecb4b8a45252e6ec597924d5" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-8360" :question/id #uuid "ef24453f-f045-5d0a-8ed3-0ca5b930bc74" :question/math-academy-id "q-8360" :question/problem "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=0\\,.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nConverting the given equation to standard form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y\\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{{2(\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}y & ={{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ and $Q(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8360/ma-source-field/dbd2b59b6454b3931876586d49499d59f1b8a6fdea15a150a89978379dccba11"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
