 {:db/id "q-83860" :question/id #uuid "497d051f-d1fb-59f1-b865-99c679ab4f76" :question/math-academy-id "q-83860" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \nThe matrix $A$ has eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=2,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=5.$\nFind a diagonal matrix $D$ and an invertible matrix $P$ such that $A=PD{P}^{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the diagonalization algorithm.\n\n**Step 1.**  Notice that we are already given the eigenvalues of the matrix: \n\n$\\,$ ${\\lambda }_{1}=2,\\,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,\\,$ ${\\lambda }_{3}=5.$ \n\n**Step 2.** Now, we need to find an eigenvector basis of $A.$ Applying our usual method, we find the following.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-2I & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-2I)x=0$ gives us the eigenverctor ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-2)I & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-(-2)I)x=0$ gives us the eigenverctor ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{3}=5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-5I & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-5I)x=0$ gives us the eigenverctor ${v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 3.** We construct the diagonal matrix $D$ and the invertible matrix $P$ in the usual way, and this gives us the following:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-83860/ma-source-field/016724adf006f2bc0051d7a70464f9739f3772e524992f0576c476fe6708bb35"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
