 {:db/id "q-84046" :question/id #uuid "1131433c-1254-58aa-b6db-67a84792b7de" :question/math-academy-id "q-84046" :question/problem "Calculate the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $9{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=9.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} & =9 \\\\ 9(0)^{2}-{y}^{2} & =9 \\\\ -{y}^{2} & =9 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot take the square root of a negative number. Therefore, the equation has no real solutions.\nSo, there are no $y$-intercepts." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-84046/ma-source-field/bc4cc11a3fa2b8ba094db568f3702389b9410dca7354cd20f8ac314afa991443"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
