 {:db/id "q-85640/ma-source-field/55864f3502a3d70aab85c0025deab19ecce67a0a94daf9d3e478036e41ad3e12" :answer-field/id #uuid "9151fede-a06c-511f-acdd-16c15e3d7d4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-85640/ma-source-field/55864f3502a3d70aab85c0025deab19ecce67a0a94daf9d3e478036e41ad3e12/b83feefa55e1e591f656e5e44ea613f9ee9af9e43d93ccb09047ca53c0556b55" "q-85640/ma-source-field/55864f3502a3d70aab85c0025deab19ecce67a0a94daf9d3e478036e41ad3e12/7d8c9373ef22b77f2fdea72d654a4f57d55459454e4c362fb52222ba82963114" "q-85640/ma-source-field/55864f3502a3d70aab85c0025deab19ecce67a0a94daf9d3e478036e41ad3e12/114e28c49a65e202077e37e1074e3fbf98826acd8b3ba78d6838c36cb1f44e5f" "q-85640/ma-source-field/55864f3502a3d70aab85c0025deab19ecce67a0a94daf9d3e478036e41ad3e12/000661f6c41e5a62caeda32ff0209de3bce4a91493fe0049047832213c48b1b4" "q-85640/ma-source-field/55864f3502a3d70aab85c0025deab19ecce67a0a94daf9d3e478036e41ad3e12/c89f8d0290db0fbed146690232ee313877697a16ed4256730e1234c580357f48"] :answer-field/correct "q-85640/ma-source-field/55864f3502a3d70aab85c0025deab19ecce67a0a94daf9d3e478036e41ad3e12/b83feefa55e1e591f656e5e44ea613f9ee9af9e43d93ccb09047ca53c0556b55" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-85640" :question/id #uuid "37e87bc7-80c8-5654-8c99-e96b9d9f6c6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-85640" :question/problem "![](images/97/97c98411b3455c78c9e061cf54fa76eabfccc369e9e364a5366eb58bd5d2935d.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the unit circle. Given that $cos⁡\\theta =\\frac{2}{7},$ what is the value of $cot⁡\\theta ?$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/8c/8c7889d63cf5894236bc5f5e24feb64ecf5a47acb2c07c807a4e65458a991232.png)\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to find $sin⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ sin⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $cos⁡\\theta =\\frac{2}{7}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sin⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{2}{7})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{4}{49}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{45}{49}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the negative answer since $sin⁡\\theta $ is negative in the fourth quadrant. So, $sin⁡\\theta =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{7}.$\n\nFinally, knowing that $cot⁡\\theta =\\frac{cos⁡\\theta }{sin⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\ncot⁡\\theta =\\frac{(\\frac{2}{7})}{(-\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{7})}=-\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{5}}=-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{15}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-85640/ma-source-field/55864f3502a3d70aab85c0025deab19ecce67a0a94daf9d3e478036e41ad3e12"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
