 {:db/id "q-86415/ma-source-field/afa84c533cd77194bba6f52902a90f17cc2fa65d7c16b381928e697cd3dc5b54" :answer-field/id #uuid "417df0a0-d7e8-5502-826d-e0777e84a95f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-86415/ma-source-field/afa84c533cd77194bba6f52902a90f17cc2fa65d7c16b381928e697cd3dc5b54/44e0c9b08665dd855fbf9cdbc85ed3508790d661cfaf5fdcfa830fb34f7e2181" "q-86415/ma-source-field/afa84c533cd77194bba6f52902a90f17cc2fa65d7c16b381928e697cd3dc5b54/db5721194d4f1c1fadb0fcb342c31b7ee5c8b71966f9b762143d7bdbae8457e8" "q-86415/ma-source-field/afa84c533cd77194bba6f52902a90f17cc2fa65d7c16b381928e697cd3dc5b54/ae8fac5318ead0983d5d2f4ed4ba74d064cd88dd70f405f57df5080c749da3da" "q-86415/ma-source-field/afa84c533cd77194bba6f52902a90f17cc2fa65d7c16b381928e697cd3dc5b54/03dbaba3c7438fd9f77f8b686e31e96a0d881ff062dc422389c7fbd9038f78b9" "q-86415/ma-source-field/afa84c533cd77194bba6f52902a90f17cc2fa65d7c16b381928e697cd3dc5b54/eb502cca3f72399b923281368104a0b2d17f7c009ce7defac6c4ed3c2d418890"] :answer-field/correct "q-86415/ma-source-field/afa84c533cd77194bba6f52902a90f17cc2fa65d7c16b381928e697cd3dc5b54/03dbaba3c7438fd9f77f8b686e31e96a0d881ff062dc422389c7fbd9038f78b9" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-86415" :question/id #uuid "211d779e-92bf-5786-beb2-56b9bec0ebf9" :question/math-academy-id "q-86415" :question/problem "The equation $-4{w}^{2}+40w-75=0$ can be written in the form $4(w+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $q,$ and solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot (-4{w}^{2}+40w-75) & =(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 4{w}^{2}-40w+75 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we move the constant term to the right-hand side, factor the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{w}^{2}-40w+75 & =0 \\\\ 4{w}^{2}-40w & =-75 \\\\ 4({w}^{2}-10w) & =-75 \\\\ 4[{w}^{2}-2\\cdot 5w+{5}^{2}-{5}^{2}] & =-75 \\\\ 4[{(w-5)}^{2}-25] & =-75\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the brackets, and write the equation in the required form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(w-5)}^{2}-4\\cdot 25 & =-75 \\\\ 4{(w-5)}^{2}-100 & =-75 \\\\ 4{(w-5)}^{2} & =-75+100 \\\\ 4{(w-5)}^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $q=25.$ We now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(w-5)}^{2} & =25 \\\\ {(w-5)}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{4} \\\\ \\sqrt{{(w-5)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{4}} \\\\ |w-5| & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ w-5 & =\\pm \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ w & =5\\pm \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w & =5+\\frac{5}{2}=\\frac{15}{2} \\\\ w & =5-\\frac{5}{2}=\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $w=\\frac{5}{2}$ and $w=\\frac{15}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-86415/ma-source-field/afa84c533cd77194bba6f52902a90f17cc2fa65d7c16b381928e697cd3dc5b54"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
